aradise. The westernmost island of the Faroes is home to innumerable puffins and many hiking trails. Mykines is one of the larger road-inaccessible islands and is only accessible via a ferry from Vágar (specifically from Sørvágur, near the airport). Ferry tickets do tend to get booked out, so make sure to book as soon as possible.","grounding":[{"source":"wikivoyage","title":"Mykines","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Mykines","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"short":"Mykines is a remote island in the Faroe Islands, open to visitors only in the summer months. The cliff walk is the whole reason to make the crossing, and Sorvagsvatn on nearby Vagar is worth adding. The island takes about four hours, June to August.","short_src":"rewrite","facts":{"visit_h":4}},"highlights":[{"id":"hl-vagar","name":"Vágar","kind":"Island","lat":62.08333,"lon":-7.26667,"dist_km":17.4,"rank_score":10.56,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Gasadalur%2C_Faroe_Islands_1.JPG/960px-Gasadalur%2C_Faroe_Islands_1.JPG","author":"Erik Christensen","licence":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licence_url":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gasadalur,_Faroe_Islands_1.JPG","w":1600,"h":1065,"ok_print":true}},{"id":"hl-sorvagsvatn","name":"Sørvágsvatn","kind":"Lake","lat":62.05,"lon":-7.23333,"dist_km":19.9,"rank_score":9.74,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/S%C3%B8rv%C3%A1gsvatn_4.jpg/960px-S%C3%B8rv%C3%A1gsvatn_4.jpg","author":"kallerna","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:S%C3%B8rv%C3%A1gsvatn_4.jpg","w":8720,"h":5000,"ok_print":true}},{"id":"hl-fjallavatn","name":"Fjallavatn","kind":"Lake","lat":62.1225,"lon":-7.29917,"dist_km":15.8,"rank_score":7.78,"resolved_by":"catalogue"},{"id":"hl-bosdalafossur","name":"Bøsdalafossur","kind":